WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.350
Audiences are split on whether Glass, the
third part of M Night Shyamalan's grounded

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.400
superhero trilogy, is a fitting conclusion
to the series.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.010
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything you need

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.630
to know about the ending to Glass and that
surprise twist, plus some crucial details

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.589
and hidden messages you might have missed.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:24.070
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care if
you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.529
Twist endings are M Night Shyamalan's trademark
and Glass is no exception with an ending that's

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:31.029
likely to be divisive among the audience.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.820
The final showdown that Mr Glass, aka Elijah
Price, has set up outside the hospital sees

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.530
The Beast take on David Dunn, who's known
as The Overseer.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.890
Elijah wants to reveal the existence of superheroes
to the world, but when Kevin and David are

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:49.309
both killed by guards called in by Sarah Paulson's
Dr Staple, the movie reveals that Dr Staple

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.980
has actually been working for a secret society
that suppresses super-powered individuals

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.780
and aims to keep their existence under wraps.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.920
The idea for this twist goes back to 1999
when Shyamalan was working on the script for

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.160
Unbreakable, and among his file of notes for
that film, he wrote down the question, 'How

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.412
come nobody knows about these superheroes?'

00:01:07.412 --> 00:01:12.860
The answer, of course, is this secret society
which has been concealing the existence of

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.890
superheroes in the world for around 10,000
years and this revelation basically confirms

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.710
Elijah's comic book theory that he expressed
in Unbreakable:

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.660
"The Egyptians drew on walls."

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.310
"Countries all over the world still pass on
knowledge through pictorial forms."

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:33.070
"I believe comics are a form of history that
someone somewhere felt or experienced."

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:38.140
Despite Kevin and David having been murdered
in Glass, Dr Staple explains to Elijah that

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:42.600
comics are wrong about secret groups being
evil because the secret society she works

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.220
for doesn't choose sides.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.520
Rather, their goal is to maintain balance
and order in society, as it's not fair to

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.100
have gods among ordinary human beings.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.770
The problem, as Dr Staple sees it, is that
whenever one super-powered individual pops

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:00.340
up, his or her opposite also then appears,
and the situation escalates.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.560
The Unbreakable, Split and Glass trilogy demonstrates
that perfectly.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.170
Unbreakable was the origin story of David
Dunn as a super-strong and powerful hero;

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:13.320
and Split, which was a secret sequel, was
about the emergence of the super-villain The

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.360
Beast.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.310
These two characters then face off directly
in spectacular fashion at the beginning of

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:22.450
Glass, with Dunn hunting down and battling
the Beast when he rescues the cheerleaders

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.120
kidnapped by the Horde.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.370
By the way, the showdown between these two
in Glass was foreshadowed all the way back

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:33.110
in Unbreakable when the young Elijah unwrapped
his first comic book "The Battle With Jaguaro".

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:38.180
Dunn, who wears a green poncho, is represented
by the caped hero on the left and the Beast,

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:42.340
aka the Horde, whose signature colour is yellow,
is Jaguaro on the right.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.380
Interestingly, in Glass, we discover that
Elijah is not only responsible for David's

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:51.200
existence as a super-powered individual but
also for the Beast because the train derailment

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.630
that Elijah caused in Unbreakable, and which
only David survived, also killed Kevin's father,

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.819
which in turn led to the creation of the Horde
inside Kevin.

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:06.770
Elijah proudly proclaims that by engineering
this event he's a mastermind who creates superheroes.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:10.450
And in another curious connection between
David and the Beast, David's son, Joseph,

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.870
went to the same school as Casey and the two
girls abducted in Split.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:20.540
Now, the way the secret society in Glass operates
is that they move from city to city identifying

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:25.340
super-powered individuals and they have a
process for dealing with them which Dr Staple

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.250
claims is "humane".

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:32.000
They begin by gaslighting the individuals,
in other words, trying to convince them that

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.420
they have delusions of grandeur as Dr Staple
attempted to do with Elijah, David and Kevin

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.380
at the psychiatric hospital.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:42.790
She almost succeeded with David and the Horde,
with David beginning to doubt his powers and

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:46.430
Patricia telling Elijah that her "horde is
losing faith".

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:51.220
The second stage that Dr Staple employs with
individuals like Mr Glass, who refuse to be

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:56.530
convinced, is to perform a kind of lobotomy
and remove or eliminate a part of their brain.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:04:00.520
She attempts the medical procedure on Elijah,
but unbeknown to her, when he broke out of

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.780
his cell the night before, he went into the
surgery room and sabotaged the equipment so

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.760
that it didn't do anything to him during the
procedure.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.690
The final stage the society undertakes in
the event of the first two failing is to completely

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:16.590
eliminate the individual which is what happens
when David and Kevin are taken out by the

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.219
society's henchmen.

00:04:18.219 --> 00:04:22.810
By the way, there was a chilling bit of foreshadowing
in one of the Glass trailers of how Dr Staple

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:26.000
held David's Dunn hand and watched on while
he was drowned in the puddle.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.590
"So you're not going to shake my hand, and
let me walk out of here."

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:33.460
And it was even foreshadowed in the scene
from Unbreakable when David says to Elijah

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.340
"Two skinny little kids were fooling around
in a pool dunking me and I swallowed some

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.340
water."

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.120
"They didn't know it, and it almost killed
me."

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.389
"Heroes don't get killed like that."

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:43.909
"Normal people do right?"

00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:47.539
And if you're unclear how the Beast could
be killed with a bullet after he survived

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:52.050
two at close range in Split, what happened
was that Casey embraced the Beast and through

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:56.729
her connection with Kevin and by saying his
full name repeatedly, Kevin was able to take

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.550
the light from the Beast.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:03.249
That meant that Kevin no longer had super-thick
skin like the Beast, so when the sniper shot

00:05:03.249 --> 00:05:06.139
him, it injured him as it would any ordinary
human being.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:11.389
In terms of who the secret society might represent,
it's not made explicit in the movie, but there

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:15.530
is a hint via the shamrock tattoo that Dr
Staple, the henchmen and the members who meet

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.779
at the restaurant have near their wrist.

00:05:17.779 --> 00:05:21.740
Clovers were considered magical plants in
Celtic culture and there are legends of Saint

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:26.250
Patrick using a three-leafed clover to explain
what the Christian holy trinity symbolised.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:30.280
If we think of clovers as having a magical
or spiritual meaning then the secret society's

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.650
clover tattoos may signify how the organisation
is dedicated to suppressing magical or god-like

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.099
powers in society.

00:05:37.099 --> 00:05:41.159
Shyamalan himself, in fact, has said that
"What makes us different is our strength"

00:05:41.159 --> 00:05:43.759
but Dr Staple "believes in the status quo."

00:05:43.759 --> 00:05:48.490
"She believes in the way that it is right
now, and she can't see past that."

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:53.120
There's still one final twist in this story,
and although Dr Staple told Elijah his theory

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.409
was right all along, it seemed like she'd
contained the situation at the hospital, even

00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:00.789
if it meant Elijah, Kevin and David all ended
up dead.

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:06.659
However, as we know, Elijah is a Lex Luthor-style
genius, and even calls himself a mastermind.

00:06:06.659 --> 00:06:11.720
And the night he broke out of his cell after
switching his sedatives for aspirin, he reprogrammed

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:15.449
the security cameras so they'd send all recorded
footage offsite.

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:19.400
Then during the breakout, Elijah deliberately
took The Beast through the basement as he

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.370
knew that area was monitored with cameras
and that the parking lot fight would all be

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.180
caught on camera too.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:29.439
In the final scenes of the movie, Elijah's
mother, Joseph and Casey receive the footage

00:06:29.439 --> 00:06:33.249
and agree to upload the evidence to the internet
for anyone to see.

00:06:33.249 --> 00:06:37.729
A couple of hours later, they meet at a location
that's been crucial throughout the trilogy:

00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:42.099
the train station, and the movie ends there
as we see the footage start to go viral, popping

00:06:42.099 --> 00:06:45.879
up on people's phones and devices and on the
TV news.

00:06:45.879 --> 00:06:50.099
And in a nice little final nod to the three
fallen supers, at the end of the film, Mrs

00:06:50.099 --> 00:06:55.520
Price, Casey, and Joseph are each dressed
in the signature colours of Elijah, purple,

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.289
Kevin, yellow, and David, green.

00:06:58.289 --> 00:07:02.770
As these scenes play, we hear Elijah's voiceover
telling us "there are unknown forces that

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.259
don't want us to realise what we are truly
capable of."

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:11.319
"I believe that if everyone sees what just
a few people become when they wholly embrace

00:07:11.319 --> 00:07:13.250
their gifts, others will awaken."

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:18.360
"Whoever these people are who don't want us
to know the truth, today they lose."

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:22.210
The real message that Shyamalan seems to want
to tell us in Glass is that difference is

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:26.949
a strength and extraordinary abilities are
within the grasp of many people.

00:07:26.949 --> 00:07:31.419
On top of that, the three films, Unbreakable,
Split and Glass, exist to prove there can

00:07:31.419 --> 00:07:35.629
be grounded and realistic superhero stories
that are different to the more fantastical

00:07:35.629 --> 00:07:40.180
superhero stories we typically see in franchises
like the Marvel Cinematic Universe and many

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.779
other comic book movies.

00:07:41.779 --> 00:07:46.770
In Unbreakable and Glass, Elijah always emphasises
that although real-life superheroes exist,

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.069
they look very different to those in comic
books.

00:07:49.069 --> 00:07:54.189
"The thing to notice about this piece... the
thing that makes it very, very special...

00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:56.369
is its realistic depiction of its figures."

00:07:56.369 --> 00:08:00.429
"When the characters reached the magazine...
they were exaggerated... as always happens."

00:08:00.429 --> 00:08:05.599
"It's all right to be afraid, David... because
this part won't be like a comic book."

00:08:05.599 --> 00:08:09.179
"Real life doesn't fit into little boxes that
were drawn for it."

00:08:09.179 --> 00:08:13.550
In Glass, at one point, Elijah says, "this
is not a cartoon […] this is the real world"

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:18.169
and, just before Pierce is killed by the Beast,
he jokes that "this is where they paint you

00:08:18.169 --> 00:08:22.469
with big eyes and bubbles of confusion above
your head."

00:08:22.469 --> 00:08:26.940
The Osaka Tower where Elijah threatens to
stage the final showdown is referred to as

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:31.159
a "true marvel", in a wink to the famous comic-book
publisher and movie studio.

00:08:31.159 --> 00:08:35.639
So, when it's revealed that Elijah's threat
is just a ruse and the showdown was always

00:08:35.639 --> 00:08:40.360
planned in the less showy setting of the hospital
car park, Shyamalan is deliberately pointing

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:45.949
out that this isn't meant to be a big-budget
superhero blockbuster with an epic CGI finale

00:08:45.949 --> 00:08:49.130
where the hero goes home after defeating the
villain.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:53.370
This choice is perhaps one of the reasons
why some viewers haven't enjoyed the movie's

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:54.370
ending.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:57.970
After all, some fans have been waiting nearly
two decades for the sequel to Unbreakable

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:02.829
and since then we've all been exposed to a
deluge of superhero movies, and big-budget

00:09:02.829 --> 00:09:07.680
comic book movies are typically the most hyped
tentpole releases right now.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.980
Glass kicked off with a thrilling start as
Dunn rescued the cheerleaders from The Beast,

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.170
but the rest of the movie played out more
like a slow-burn psychological thriller.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:20.529
And I suspect some in the audience were indeed
hoping for the final showdown to take place

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:21.810
on the Osaka Tower.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:26.330
So, when instead two of the main characters
are killed in a much more understated fashion

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:31.240
by some nameless henchman from a secret society,
that's bound to provoke a reaction.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:35.250
The thing is, though, that's what the movie
wants to do; it's pointing out that real-life

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:40.940
heroes and villains don't have these epic
fights, and these characters aren't invincible.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:45.080
The low-key nature of the final showdown in
Glass is also in keeping with the feel of

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.329
both Unbreakable and Split, so it would have
been odd for the film to suddenly pivot to

00:09:49.329 --> 00:09:52.610
an epic climax on top of a shiny skyscraper.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:58.149
The movie intends to subvert flashy superhero
tropes and instead prove that the big spectacles

00:09:58.149 --> 00:10:02.819
we see on film or in comic books are just
an exaggerated version of more realistic yet

00:10:02.819 --> 00:10:05.930
still extraordinary powers people can have
in real life.

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:10.990
In light of this, it's also interesting that
on her desk, Dr Staple has a book by Euripides,

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:15.870
a playwright in ancient Greece whose tragedies
are often noted for their realistically drawn

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:21.050
characters, psychological realism, and mythical
heroes portrayed as ordinary people living

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.550
through extraordinary situations.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:28.209
Glass doesn't achieve the brilliance of Unbreakable
and falls into Shyamalan's trap of inserting

00:10:28.209 --> 00:10:31.089
too much exposition into the mouths of his
characters.

00:10:31.089 --> 00:10:35.259
There's an overabundance of explaining literally
what we've just seen or are about to see on

00:10:35.259 --> 00:10:39.750
screen, for example, when Mrs Price comes
on to tell us that this is "what they call

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:44.029
the showdown", it seems a pretty redundant
line to have in a movie released in 2019,

00:10:44.029 --> 00:10:48.600
given that almost everyone will be familiar
with comic book movies by now.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.360
And Shyamalan has some great actors in this
film, but his insistence on sticking firmly

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:57.290
to his script and generally not allowing actors
to improvise, also seems to lead to some rather

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.290
clunky lines.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:03.879
Something that fans are inevitably interested
in is whether Glass represents the final chapter

00:11:03.879 --> 00:11:05.730
in the Unbreakable and Split universe.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:10.139
Obviously, all the main characters are dead,
however, the final scene implies we'll see

00:11:10.139 --> 00:11:14.630
new heroes and villains emerge and any of
those could be explored in future movies or

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.089
a TV show.

00:11:16.089 --> 00:11:20.670
So far, Shyamalan has said he's not particularly
keen for another follow up as, with the exception

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.430
of this trilogy, he generally doesn't do sequels.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:27.880
Glass is also supposed to be a satisfying
conclusion to the series and, for me, it seems

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:33.490
in keeping with the idea of a grounded superhero
series not to expand it out into a much larger

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:34.490
franchise.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:37.370
Now, what do you think about the end of Glass?

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.529
And what were your favourite or least favourite
parts of the movie?

00:11:40.529 --> 00:11:42.370
Let me know in the comments below.

